From 7b844f2fc5813a72a0e0a5616a7a2efabb59c74a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 17:16:40 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(machines): Tormach 8L and 15L Slant-PRO lathe
 definitions

Two shipped lathe machines from Tormach's public spec sheets, so
turning programs are judged against a real Tormach lathe envelope and
can be checked in PathPilot Hub's 8L / 15L:

- 8L: X 4.5 in, Z 10 in, 180-2500 / 350-5000 rpm (two ranges, 5C),
  150 IPM, 99-entry tool table (gang / QCTP).
- 15L Slant-PRO: X 10 in, Z 12 in, 180-2500 rpm (6 in chuck), 60 IPM,
  8-station turret.

Inch, full-stroke-either-way travel like the shipped Tormach mills.
The 8L's 4.5 in X and the 15L's chuck-rated 2500 rpm are the
conservative readings; sources and choices in the decision record.
Pinned by tormach_lathes (2 tests).

Fixes #611

